 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "tree is the level-order serialization used for N-ary trees: the root value, then null, then for each node in breadth-first order its children's values followed by null (trailing nulls omitted). A path [p0, ..., pL-1] matches a chain of nodes v0, ..., vL-1 where each v(i+1) is a child of v(i) and each value equals its path entry. Variant 1: return true when some matching chain starts at the root (it may stop before a leaf), else false.",
